  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The `habeas-evidence` skill MUST tell agents not to write placeholder evidence when a requirement's or example's implementation is pending. The text names no other modes or boundaries.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_never_writes_placeholder_evidence_for_pending_work]` is marked `{test}` and covers it. It finds the numbered step of the `habeas-evidence` skill workflow that contains \"Stop and report each finding that needs the user\". It does this through the helpers `step_of` and `step`. It then calls `assert_text_in_order` on that step's text. That helper panics unless \"names only implementation that is still pending\" appears, followed later by \"never write placeholder evidence\".\n\nThe search result for `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` shows the matching text in step 5. It says a missing record or false judgment whose rationale names only implementation that is still pending is expected, and \"never write placeholder evidence\". The assertion therefore ties the prohibition to the pending-implementation case. It would fail if the prohibition were dropped, reworded, moved to another step, or detached from the pending case.\n\nI did not read `workflow_steps`. I relied on the `SKILL.md` excerpt, which shows both phrases within step 5.\n\nNo gaps found. There are no acknowledgments.",
